{"parentUuid":"5a5c3c4c-6eb4-475d-9174-a4d54819d91c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CebHCtyLL1UhV2kp6E2rm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both are live on your console now, and the 8-concurrent timing run is being monitored:\n\n**On the UI (as you asked):**\n- **Runs tab** → `sf-discover-full-647` is **RUNNING** at the top (it'll fill in duration + rows as it goes, and its detail page shows per-object timing thanks to the #645 per-row metric).\n- **Templates tab** → `sf-discover-full-647` shows **LAUNCHED**, live **v1**, described as *\"21-object Salesforce→BQ full sync, fields auto-discovered (#647)\"* — you can re-trigger it from there anytime.\n\n**Why the switch to serve:** running it *through* the console (I registered the generated config as a template, launched v1, and triggered it) is what makes it appear on the UI — the CLI runs never register with serve. This one serve run does triple duty: it's the **8-concurrent timing run** you wanted, it's **visible on Runs**, and as it completes each object it records to the catalog so it'll also populate the **Datasets** and **Lineage** tabs.\n\nI stopped the CLI timing run before triggering so the two wouldn't race on the same overwrite tables.\n\nA background monitor is watching the serve run; when it finishes I'll report the **8-concurrent wall time vs the ~28 min at 5-concurrent**, confirm the 4.8M total, and grab a final screenshot showing the completed run plus the populated Datasets/Lineage. It's running at 8 concurrent now."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1395,"cache_read_input_tokens":790827,"output_tokens":774,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":282},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1395,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference