{"parentUuid":"3accbd75-6b6c-4fe1-8188-02b347f7b2d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CebKF28EW337Hb7uG79iW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3610,"cache_read_input_tokens":815050,"output_tokens":1036,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":305},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3610,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1036,"cache_read_input_tokens":815050,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3610},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CebKEdgN2hmtxohE7HFBQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"de1c67b3-f0d3-493f-af30-f8985e75f53e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:40:29.864Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"feat/native-byte-passthrough-633","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"de1c67b3-f0d3-493f-af30-f8985e75f53e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CebKF28EW337Hb7uG79iW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed (`5bab3fce`). Now — you're right, and I got the shape wrong. I baked the fully-expanded matrix (every object's SELECT + sink) into the template instead of keeping it generic with the object list as a param. Let me be straight about *why* a plain param doesn't drop in, because it's an architectural thing, not just a config tweak:\n\n**A serve template runs its stored config verbatim — there's no `discover` step at trigger time.** And SOQL has no `SELECT *`, so each object's full field list *must* be materialized into the matrix before a run can execute. Those two facts together force the template to be pre-expanded — which is exactly the baked columns/sinks you saw.\n\nSo \"object list is a param\" splits into two very different things:\n\n1. **Param at *generate* time (easy, today):** make the discovery config's `salesforce.objects` a `${param.objects}` and add `--param` to `faucet discover`, so one generic config generates a matrix for any object set:\n   `faucet discover salesforce.yaml --param objects=\"Account,Contact,Lead\" -o gen.yaml`\n   The connection template stays generic; you regenerate when the object set or schema changes. But the thing that *runs/registers* is still the generated matrix.\n\n2. **Param at *trigger* time (the real generic template, not built):** register **one** generic template, and passing `objects` at trigger makes serve **discover the fields and fan out at run time** — no regenerate, new fields/objects picked up automatically. This is the *dynamic fan-out* layer of #647 (I filed it; the discovery *primitive* exists now, but the trigger-time discover-and-expand does not). It's a real executor+serve feature — the run would describe the param'd objects, build each SELECT, and expand the matrix on the fly.\n\n**(2) is clearly what you're describing, and it's the right end-state.** It's a substantial build (runtime discovery + dynamic matrix expansion + a list-typed param), so before I spend on it I want to make sure I build the right shape: do you want me to go straight for (2) — the generic template where `objects` is a trigger param and fields auto-discover at run time — or wire up (1) now as an interim while (2) lands? I'd default to building (2)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3610,"cache_read_input_tokens":815050,"output_tokens":1036,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":305},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3610,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1036,"cache_read_input_tokens":815050,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3610},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CebKEdgN2hmtxohE7HFBQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"4ce98f54-6963-4543-9d83-e099c56d84a3","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:40:40.893Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"feat/native-byte-passthrough-633","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
