{"parentUuid":"16523755-9235-4646-9dbf-d03ed3ac1653","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CebKaRzxVQhEVZft5yeC9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3000,"cache_read_input_tokens":820882,"output_tokens":2074,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1281},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3000,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2074,"cache_read_input_tokens":820882,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3000},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CebKa3XqwbMZaQJhSjxun","type":"assistant","uuid":"c2a26f7c-6a6b-4494-b5fc-32b65168de3e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:45:05.639Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"feat/native-byte-passthrough-633","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"c2a26f7c-6a6b-4494-b5fc-32b65168de3e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CebKaRzxVQhEVZft5yeC9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the **8-concurrent** result — and it's an interesting (and honest) finding:\n\n## 8-concurrent: 32.8 min · 4,804,086 rows (21/21) — *not faster than 5-concurrent (28.7 min)*\n\n| concurrency | wall time | total rows |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5 | 28.7 min | 4,803,842 |\n| **8** | **32.8 min** | **4,804,086** |\n\nMore concurrency **didn't help — it was marginally slower.** The reason is in the per-object breakdown (makespan drivers):\n\n| time | object | rows |\n|---:|---|---:|\n| 29.8 min | Lead | 605,094 |\n| 28.3 min | Contact | 483,060 |\n| 20.1 min | Opportunity | 221,044 |\n| 15.7 min | SBQQ__QuoteLine__c | 295,840 |\n\n**The makespan is set by the single slowest object, not by faucet's parallelism.** Lead alone takes ~28–30 min inside Salesforce's Bulk API 2.0 export (submit → server-side query → fetch) — and no amount of faucet concurrency shrinks one object's export. With only 21 objects, 5 slots already start all the big ones simultaneously; adding slots (8) just lets the *small* objects start sooner, and they finish in seconds anyway. The ~4-min delta between the two runs is within Salesforce's own export-time variance (and 8 concurrent Bulk jobs may brush against Salesforce's server-side job limits).\n\n**Takeaway:** for a Salesforce Bulk sync, concurrency past ~5 buys nothing — the bottleneck is Salesforce's per-object export throughput, not faucet. The real lever would be **splitting the largest objects** (PK-range sharding *within* Lead/Contact so one object exports in parallel chunks), not more matrix concurrency.\n\nThe run is on your console: **Runs** shows it completed with its duration, and its **detail page** shows `template: sf-discover-full-647 v1` (the provenance I just added).\n\n---\n\nStill awaiting your steer on the earlier question: for the **generic template with `objects` as a param**, do you want me to build option **(2)** — trigger-time discovery + dynamic fan-out (the real generic template) — or wire **(1)** the generate-time param as an interim first? I'd default to (2)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3000,"cache_read_input_tokens":820882,"output_tokens":2074,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1281},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3000,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2074,"cache_read_input_tokens":820882,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3000},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CebKa3XqwbMZaQJhSjxun","type":"assistant","uuid":"4c77e3f8-56e5-4390-a85d-cf98bcef27df","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:45:15.874Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"feat/native-byte-passthrough-633","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
