{"parentUuid":"5ce640ba-9e27-4977-98e1-24f3211b0e5a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CebqErkfeSi3p92CMb8i1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clippy clean. Let me add the run-time fan-out to the REST README docs, then commit everything:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_read_input_tokens":875943,"output_tokens":1656,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":426},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1656,"cache_read_input_tokens":875943,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CebqEUgcnVEbaWCsADamK","type":"assistant","uuid":"e5291d8d-fe04-4471-8c21-65f2acc3d885","timestamp":"2026-09-01T01:13:54.432Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"feat/native-byte-passthrough-633","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"e5291d8d-fe04-4471-8c21-65f2acc3d885","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CebqErkfeSi3p92CMb8i1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TRfBopyXdeqEtUSGUZCfzE","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream/crates/source/rest/README.md","old_string":"| Field | Type | Default | Description |\n|-------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `objects` | array<string> | `[]` | Explicit objects to discover (e.g. `[Account, Contact, Churn__c]`). Empty ⇒ scan the global describe and take every queryable object. Naming them keeps the connection template generic. |\n| `api_version` | string | `v60.0` | REST API version for the describe calls. |\n| `operation` | `queryAll \\| query` | `queryAll` | Bulk-query operation baked into each object's SOQL (`queryAll` includes soft-deleted rows). |\n| `route_by_table_id` | bool | `true` | Also emit `sink: { config: { table_id: <snake object> } }` per row so a fan-out lands one table per object (table-based sinks). Set `false` for file sinks. |","new_string":"| Field | Type | Default | Description |\n|-------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `objects` | array<string> **or** string | `[]` | Objects to discover — a list (`[Account, Contact]`) or a comma-separated string (`\"Account,Contact\"`) so a single run-param can drive it (`objects: \"${param.objects}\"`). Empty, or `\"all\"`, ⇒ every queryable object. |\n| `fan_out` | bool | `false` | **Run-time** fan-out: when `true`, `faucet run` / `faucet serve` discovers the objects' fields and generates the matrix *at run time* — so one generic template (`objects: \"${param.objects}\"`, no `matrix:`) syncs any object set passed at trigger, fields resolved live. When `false`, the block only affects `faucet discover`. |\n| `sink_ref` | string / null | `default` | With `fan_out`, the sink template (under `pipeline.sinks`) each object routes to. |\n| `api_version` | string | `v60.0` | REST API version for the describe calls. |\n| `operation` | `queryAll \\| query` | `queryAll` | Bulk-query operation baked into each object's SOQL (`queryAll` includes soft-deleted rows). |\n| `route_by_table_id` | bool | `true` | Also emit `sink: { config: { table_id: <snake object> } }` per row so a fan-out lands one table per object (table-based sinks). Set `false` for file sinks. |\n\n**Two ways to use it.** *Generate-time* (`faucet discover`, `fan_out: false`) writes a static matrix you review/commit. *Run-time* (`fan_out: true`) skips the generate step — register one generic template with `objects` as a param and it discovers + fans out on every trigger, picking up new fields automatically:\n\n```yaml\nsource:\n  type: rest\n  config:\n    base_url: \"https://acme.my.salesforce.com\"\n    auth: { type: token_endpoint, config: { … } }\n    salesforce: { fan_out: true, objects: \"${param.objects}\", sink_ref: bigquery }\n# no matrix: — generated live from `objects` at run time\n```\n```console\n$ faucet run salesforce.yaml --param objects=\"Account,Contact,Lead\"   # or \"all\"\n```"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_read_input_tokens":875943,"output_tokens":1656,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":426},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1656,"cache_read_input_tokens":875943,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CebqEUgcnVEbaWCsADamK","type":"assistant","uuid":"d7becdfe-27d4-403b-994a-5d26b3a2a3c1","timestamp":"2026-09-01T01:14:06.496Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"feat/native-byte-passthrough-633","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"d7becdfe-27d4-403b-994a-5d26b3a2a3c1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"58dfe3bd-5765-4c89-8195-2459dbc080b5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TRfBopyXdeqEtUSGUZCfzE","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream/crates/source/rest/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"95510316-678e-4c86-9650-7558f2385009","timestamp":"2026-09-01T01:14:06.853Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream/crates/source/rest/README.md","oldString":"| Field | Type | Default | Description |\n|-------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `objects` | array<string> | `[]` | Explicit objects to discover (e.g. `[Account, Contact, Churn__c]`). Empty ⇒ scan the global describe and take every queryable object. Naming them keeps the connection template generic. |\n| `api_version` | string | `v60.0` | REST API version for the describe calls. |\n| `operation` | `queryAll \\| query` | `queryAll` | Bulk-query operation baked into each object's SOQL (`queryAll` includes soft-deleted rows). |\n| `route_by_table_id` | bool | `true` | Also emit `sink: { config: { table_id: <snake object> } }` per row so a fan-out lands one table per object (table-based sinks). Set `false` for file sinks. |","newString":"| Field | Type | Default | Description |\n|-------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `objects` | array<string> **or** string | `[]` | Objects to discover — a list (`[Account, Contact]`) or a comma-separated string (`\"Account,Contact\"`) so a single run-param can drive it (`objects: \"${param.objects}\"`). Empty, or `\"all\"`, ⇒ every queryable object. |\n| `fan_out` | bool | `false` | **Run-time** fan-out: when `true`, `faucet run` / `faucet serve` discovers the objects' fields and generates the matrix *at run time* — so one generic template (`objects: \"${param.objects}\"`, no `matrix:`) syncs any object set passed at trigger, fields resolved live. When `false`, the block only affects `faucet discover`. |\n| `sink_ref` | string / null | `default` | With `fan_out`, the sink template (under `pipeline.sinks`) each object routes to. |\n| `api_version` | string | `v60.0` | REST API version for the describe calls. |\n| `operation` | `queryAll \\| query` | `queryAll` | Bulk-query operation baked into each object's SOQL (`queryAll` includes soft-deleted rows). |\n| `route_by_table_id` | bool | `true` | Also emit `sink: { config: { table_id: <snake object> } }` per row so a fan-out lands one table per object (table-based sinks). Set `false` for file sinks. |\n\n**Two ways to use it.** *Generate-time* (`faucet discover`, `fan_out: false`) writes a static matrix you review/commit. *Run-time* (`fan_out: true`) skips the generate step — register one generic template with `objects` as a param and it discovers + fans out on every trigger, picking up new fields automatically:\n\n```yaml\nsource:\n  type: rest\n  config:\n    base_url: \"https://acme.my.salesforce.com\"\n    auth: { type: token_endpoint, config: { … } }\n    salesforce: { fan_out: true, objects: \"${param.objects}\", sink_ref: bigquery }\n# no matrix: — generated live from `objects` at run time\n```\n```console\n$ faucet run salesforce.yaml --param objects=\"Account,Contact,Lead\"   # or \"all\"\n```","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":312,"oldLines":17,"newStart":312,"newLines":34,"lines":[" "," | Field | Type | Default | Description |"," |-------|------|---------|-------------|","-| `objects` | array<string> | `[]` | Explicit objects to discover (e.g. `[Account, Contact, Churn__c]`). Empty ⇒ scan the global describe and take every queryable object. Naming them keeps the connection template generic. |","+| `objects` | array<string> **or** string | `[]` | Objects to discover — a list (`[Account, Contact]`) or a comma-separated string (`\"Account,Contact\"`) so a single run-param can drive it (`objects: \"${param.objects}\"`). Empty, or `\"all\"`, ⇒ every queryable object. |","+| `fan_out` | bool | `false` | **Run-time** fan-out: when `true`, `faucet run` / `faucet serve` discovers the objects' fields and generates the matrix *at run time* — so one generic template (`objects: \"${param.objects}\"`, no `matrix:`) syncs any object set passed at trigger, fields resolved live. When `false`, the block only affects `faucet discover`. |","+| `sink_ref` | string / null | `default` | With `fan_out`, the sink template (under `pipeline.sinks`) each object routes to. |"," | `api_version` | string | `v60.0` | REST API version for the describe calls. |"," | `operation` | `queryAll \\| query` | `queryAll` | Bulk-query operation baked into each object's SOQL (`queryAll` includes soft-deleted rows). |"," | `route_by_table_id` | bool | `true` | Also emit `sink: { config: { table_id: <snake object> } }` per row so a fan-out lands one table per object (table-based sinks). Set `false` for file sinks. |"," ","+**Two ways to use it.** *Generate-time* (`faucet discover`, `fan_out: false`) writes a static matrix you review/commit. *Run-time* (`fan_out: true`) skips the generate step — register one generic template with `objects` as a param and it discovers + fans out on every trigger, picking up new fields automatically:","+"," ```yaml"," source:","   type: rest","   config:","     base_url: \"https://acme.my.salesforce.com\"","     auth: { type: token_endpoint, config: { … } }","+    salesforce: { fan_out: true, objects: \"${param.objects}\", sink_ref: bigquery }","+# no matrix: — generated live from `objects` at run time","+```","+```console","+$ faucet run salesforce.yaml --param objects=\"Account,Contact,Lead\"   # or \"all\"","+```","+","+```yaml","+source:","+  type: rest","+  config:","+    base_url: \"https://acme.my.salesforce.com\"","+    auth: { type: token_endpoint, config: { … } }","     salesforce: { objects: [Account, Contact, Opportunity] }"," ```"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d7becdfe-27d4-403b-994a-5d26b3a2a3c1","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"feat/native-byte-passthrough-633","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
